  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protected area conservation of eastern chimpanzees, western equatoria, South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to establish and sustain an effective conservation management and antipoaching presence by the Ministry of Wildlife Conservation and Tourism (MWCT) in the Game Reserves of Western Equatoria State, South Sudan for the purpose of protecting eastern chimpanzees. The recipient will develop an anti-poaching presence in the Game Reserves through the development of a basic network of access roads for deployment of rangers and general management and oversight of rangers; lay the foundation for future survey and monitoring efforts for eastern chimpanzees in the Game Reserves and neighbouring areas; work with the South Sudanese Ministry for Wildlife, Conservation, and Tourism (MWCT) to clarify and codify the legal boundaries of the Game Reserves and to identify other adjoining areas deserving protection; and establish the basis for long term conservation management and anti-poaching of the Game Reserves.</narrative>
  </description>
